<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>EOB extraction eval — {{ generated_at }}</title>
<style>
  :root { --ink:#16191d; --muted:#6b7280; --line:#e3e5e8; --bg:#ffffff;
          --warn-bg:#fff4e5; --warn-line:#c2761a; --bad-bg:#fdecea; --bad-line:#b3261e;
          --ok-bg:#e9f6ef; --ok-line:#0f7b46; }
  * { box-sizing:border-box; }
  body { margin:0; padding:0 20px 80px; background:var(--bg); color:var(--ink);
         font:16px/1.6 -apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,"Segoe UI",Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif; }
  .wrap { max-width:980px; margin:0 auto; }
  h1 { font-size:28px; margin:36px 0 6px; letter-spacing:-0.01em; }
  h2 { font-size:21px; margin:44px 0 10px; padding-top:14px; border-top:1px solid var(--line); }
  h3 { font-size:16px; margin:22px 0 6px; }
  p.sub { color:var(--muted); margin:0 0 22px; }
  table { border-collapse:collapse; width:100%; margin:14px 0; font-size:14px; }
  th,td { text-align:left; padding:8px 10px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); }
  th { font-weight:600; color:var(--muted); font-size:12px; text-transform:uppercase;
       letter-spacing:0.04em; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align:right; font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums; }
  .banner { padding:16px 18px; border-radius:8px; margin:20px 0; border-left:5px solid; }
  .banner.ok   { background:var(--ok-bg);   border-color:var(--ok-line); }
  .banner.warn { background:var(--warn-bg); border-color:var(--warn-line); }
  .banner.bad  { background:var(--bad-bg);  border-color:var(--bad-line); }
  .banner h2 { border:0; margin:0 0 6px; padding:0; font-size:17px; }
  .chart { display:block; margin:10px 0 4px; }
  .tick { font-size:11px; fill:#6b7280; }
  .axis-label { font-size:12px; fill:#3a3f46; }
  .point-label { font-size:12px; fill:#16191d; font-weight:600; }
  .cell-light { font-size:12px; fill:#16191d; }
  .cell-dark  { font-size:12px; fill:#ffffff; }
  .cell-null  { font-size:11px; fill:#9ca3af; }
  .legend, .note { color:var(--muted); font-size:13px; margin:4px 0 18px; }
  code, pre { font-family:ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace; font-size:12.5px; }
  pre { background:#f6f7f9; padding:14px; border-radius:6px; overflow-x:auto;
        white-space:pre-wrap; word-break:break-word; }
  details { border:1px solid var(--line); border-radius:6px; padding:10px 14px; margin:10px 0; }
  summary { cursor:pointer; font-weight:600; }
  .pill { display:inline-block; padding:1px 8px; border-radius:99px; font-size:12px;
          border:1px solid var(--line); color:var(--muted); }
  .pill.opt { background:var(--ok-bg); border-color:var(--ok-line); color:var(--ok-line); }
  .zero { color:var(--muted); }
</style>
</head>
<body><div class="wrap">

<h1>EOB extraction evaluation</h1>
<p class="sub">
  Generated {{ generated_at }} · harness v{{ harness_version }} ·
  suite {{ suite_size }} tasks · {{ headline|length }} run(s)
</p>
<table>
  <tr><th>run</th><th>adapter</th><th>model</th><th>commit</th><th>prompt</th></tr>
  {% for row in headline %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ row.short_id }}</code></td>
    <td>{{ row.adapter }}</td>
    <td><code>{{ row.model_id }}</code></td>
    <td><code>{{ row.git_commit }}</code>{% if row.git_dirty %}
        <span class="pill">dirty tree — not reproducible</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td><code>{{ row.prompt }}</code></td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

{# Calibration sits above every score on purpose: the reader should learn
   how far the judge can be trusted before seeing numbers that depend on it. #}
{% if calibration %}
<div class="banner ok">
  <h2>Judge calibration</h2>
  <p style="margin:0">
    Cohen's kappa <strong>{{ "%.3f"|format(calibration.kappa) if calibration.kappa is not none else "undefined" }}</strong>
    {% if calibration.kappa_ci_low is not none %}
      [{{ "%.3f"|format(calibration.kappa_ci_low) }}, {{ "%.3f"|format(calibration.kappa_ci_high) }}]
    {% endif %}
    — <strong>{{ calibration.band }}</strong>, over {{ calibration.n }} labelled items.
    Human self-agreement ceiling
    {{ "%.3f"|format(calibration.human_ceiling_kappa) if calibration.human_ceiling_kappa is not none else "not measured" }}
    (from {{ calibration.human_ceiling_n }} repeated items).
  </p>
  <p class="note" style="margin:8px 0 0">
    Read the judge's kappa against the ceiling, not against 1.0: no human labels
    perfectly consistently, so the ceiling bounds what any judge could reach.
  </p>
</div>
{% else %}
<div class="banner bad">
  <h2>No calibration for this judge rubric</h2>
  <p style="margin:0">
    Rubric <code>{{ rubric_hash }}</code>: {{ calibration_problem }}.
    Any judge-adjusted figure below is of <strong>unknown reliability</strong>
    and must not be reported as a measurement.
  </p>
  <p class="note" style="margin:8px 0 0">
    Produce one with <code>scripts/label.py --new</code> then
    <code>scripts/calibrate.py --save</code>.
  </p>
</div>
{% endif %}

<h2>Headline comparison</h2>
<p class="sub">Every figure carries a 95% bootstrap interval over tasks.</p>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>run</th><th>adapter</th><th class="num">n</th><th class="num">schema</th>
    <th class="num">mean F1 [95% CI]</th><th class="num">cost</th>
    <th class="num">$/task</th><th class="num">failures</th>
  </tr>
  {% for row in headline %}
  <tr>
    <td><code>{{ row.short_id }}</code></td>
    <td>{{ row.adapter }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ row.n }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.2f"|format(row.schema_pass_rate) }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(row.f1) }}
        [{{ "%.3f"|format(row.f1_low) }}, {{ "%.3f"|format(row.f1_high) }}]</td>
    <td class="num">${{ "%.4f"|format(row.cost) }}</td>
    <td class="num">${{ "%.6f"|format(row.cost_per_task) }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ row.failures }}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>Cost against quality</h2>
<p class="sub">Which runs are worth their price, rather than which scored highest.</p>
{{ scatter_svg|safe }}
<table>
  <tr><th>run</th><th class="num">$/task</th><th class="num">mean F1</th><th>frontier</th></tr>
  {% for point in frontier %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ point.label }}</td>
    <td class="num">${{ "%.6f"|format(point.cost_per_task) }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(point.quality) }}</td>
    <td>{% if point.pareto_optimal %}<span class="pill opt">on the frontier</span>
        {% else %}<span class="pill">dominated by {{ point.dominated_by|join(", ") }}</span>
        {% endif %}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>

<h2>By category</h2>
<p class="sub">
  Exploratory. These are many comparisons on one dataset; treat them as
  directions to look, not findings.
</p>
{{ heatmap_svg|safe }}

<h2>By field</h2>
<p class="sub">
  Which fields drag which models down. Hallucination is reported separately,
  against the cases where the document genuinely had no value — the only
  cases where a value can be invented.
</p>
{% for field in fields %}
<h3><code>{{ field.field }}</code></h3>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>adapter</th><th class="num">correct</th><th class="num">wrong</th>
    <th class="num">missed</th><th class="num">hallucinated</th>
    <th class="num">hallucination rate</th>
  </tr>
  {% for run in field.per_run %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ run.adapter }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ run.correct }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ run.wrong }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ run.missed }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ run.hallucinated }}</td>
    <td class="num">
      {% if run.hallucination_rate is not none %}
        {{ "%.1f"|format(run.hallucination_rate * 100) }}%
        <span class="zero">({{ run.hallucinated }}/{{ run.nullable_cases }})</span>
      {% else %}—{% endif %}
    </td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% endfor %}

<h2>Paired comparisons</h2>
{% if comparisons %}
<p class="sub">
  Both models see identical tasks, so the comparison is paired and the
  task-to-task variation cancels.
</p>
{{ comparison_chart|safe }}
<table>
  <tr>
    <th>comparison</th><th class="num">n</th><th class="num">difference [95% CI]</th>
    <th class="num">McNemar p</th><th class="num">Holm p</th><th>verdict</th>
  </tr>
  {% for c in comparisons %}
  <tr>
    <td>{{ c.label }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ c.n }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%+.4f"|format(c.diff) }}
        [{{ "%+.4f"|format(c.low) }}, {{ "%+.4f"|format(c.high) }}]</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(c.p_raw) }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ "%.3f"|format(c.p_holm) }}</td>
    <td>{% if c.spans_zero %}<span class="zero">not distinguishable from zero</span>
        {% else %}{{ c.verdict }}{% endif %}</td>
  </tr>
  {% endfor %}
</table>
{% else %}
<p class="note">Only one run — nothing to compare against.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Failures</h2>
<p class="sub">
  Every task any run scored below 1.0, with the document, the answer key,
  and each model's output.
</p>
{% if failures %}
{% for failure in failures %}
<details>
  <summary>{{ failure.task_id }} — {{ failure.category }}</summary>
  <h3>Document</h3>
  <pre>{{ failure.document }}</pre>
  <h3>Expected</h3>
  <pre>{{ failure.expected }}</pre>
  {% for run in failure.runs %}
  <h3>{{ run.adapter }}{% if run.f1 is not none %} — F1 {{ "%.3f"|format(run.f1) }}{% endif %}</h3>
  {% if run.error %}<p class="note">Task errored: <code>{{ run.error }}</code></p>{% endif %}
  {% if run.bad_fields %}
  <table>
    <tr><th>field</th><th>outcome</th><th>judge verdict</th><th>judge reasoning</th></tr>
    {% for field, outcome in run.bad_fields.items() %}
    <tr>
      <td><code>{{ field }}</code></td>
      <td>{{ outcome }}</td>
      <td>{{ run.judge[field].verdict if run.judge.get(field) else "—" }}</td>
      <td>{{ run.judge[field].reason if run.judge.get(field) else "—" }}</td>
    </tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  {% endif %}
  <pre>{{ run.response_text }}</pre>
  {% endfor %}
</details>
{% endfor %}
{% else %}
<p class="note">No run scored below 1.0 on any task.</p>
{% endif %}

<h2>Methods</h2>

<h3>Task suite</h3>
<table>
  <tr><th>category</th><th class="num">tasks</th></tr>
  {% for name, count in task_distribution %}
  <tr><td>{{ name }}</td><td class="num">{{ count }}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  <tr><td><strong>total</strong></td><td class="num"><strong>{{ suite_size }}</strong></td></tr>
</table>

<h3>Scoring</h3>
<p>
  Micro-averaged precision, recall and F1 over the eight schema fields. A value
  that is wrong counts as both a false positive and a false negative, since a
  confidently wrong answer is worse than an abstention. A value invented where
  the document has none is a false positive. Correctly-null fields are excluded
  from the average so that leaving nullable fields empty cannot inflate a score.
</p>

<h3>Document provenance</h3>
<p>
  Documents in the failure gallery are read from the task files on disk, not
  from the run record. If a task has been edited since a run, the document
  shown is the current one while the scores are the historical ones. The
  commit recorded against each run above identifies which version was
  actually evaluated.
</p>

<h3>Normalization</h3>
<pre>{{ normalization_rules }}</pre>

<h3>Judge rubric (verbatim)</h3>
<pre>{{ rubric_text }}</pre>

<h3>Statistics</h3>
<p>
  Intervals are percentile bootstrap, {{ bootstrap_iterations }} iterations,
  seed {{ bootstrap_seed }}, resampling <em>tasks</em> rather than fields — the
  eight fields of a task come from one document and fail together, so
  resampling fields would treat correlated observations as independent and
  produce intervals far too narrow. Comparisons are paired, since every model
  sees identical tasks. Per-category p-values are Holm-corrected across the
  comparison family.
</p>
<p>
  At n={{ n_tasks }} and a baseline of {{ "%.2f"|format(baseline) }}, the
  unpaired minimum detectable effect is {{ "%.3f"|format(mde) }}. The paired
  comparisons above resolve considerably finer differences, because both models
  see the same tasks and most per-task differences are exactly zero.
</p>

<h3>Calibration</h3>
<p>
  {% if calibration %}
    Cohen's kappa against blind human labels, bootstrap interval, and an
    intra-rater ceiling from double-labelled items. Kappa is reported rather
    than raw agreement because raw agreement is inflated by whichever class
    dominates.
  {% else %}
    Not performed for rubric <code>{{ rubric_hash }}</code>. Judge-adjusted
    figures in this report are uncalibrated.
  {% endif %}
</p>

</div></body>
</html>
